# Story 94: Secret Redaction (45s)
# Hook: Your secrets never leave your machine -- redaction happens before output is shared.
# Duration: 45s
# Source: story-094-secret-redaction.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 6

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Your secrets never leave your machine -- redaction happens before output is shared.

[00:03.0 --> 00:09.0]
Start rysh. Suppose your terminal output contains an API key or token -- exactly the thing you don't want to broadcast.

[00:09.0 --> 00:18.0]
Double-Escape into rysh mode. ##private pane print shows the raw buffer -- everything, secrets included, on your screen.

[00:18.0 --> 00:28.0]
##public pane print shows the redacted version -- the same view the SharedOutputActor forwards upstream. Secrets are masked.

[00:28.0 --> 00:38.0]
When you share a pane, the SharedOutputActor redacts before output leaves the session, so the server never sees raw secrets.

[00:38.0 --> 00:45.0]
Redaction plus a command blocklist means collaboration without leaking credentials. Share with confidence.

